Task 13 plan is approved with the following required corrections.

1. Correct the rate-limit counting semantics.

The proposed DrawingRateLimiter code checks:

    if (current count >= maxActions)
        reject with 429
    else
        increment

Therefore requests after the quota is exhausted are rejected but are NOT
added to the counter.

Use and document this behavior consistently:

    requests 1..50 -> counted and allowed
    request 51+   -> rejected with 429, counter remains 50
    window expires -> next request starts a new window

Authenticated mutation attempts that are still within the available quota
consume quota even if business processing later returns 400/404/409/500.

Do not claim that the 51st rejected request increments the counter.

2. Fix the memory-cleanup description and implementation.

The currently proposed lazy reset is not bounded memory because users who
never return leave entries in the ConcurrentHashMap indefinitely.

Implement a small opportunistic cleanup mechanism without adding a scheduler
or dependency.

The goal is simply to periodically remove entries whose windows have
expired.

Keep the implementation simple and thread-safe.

Do not introduce Redis or a cache library.

Document the cleanup strategy and its approximate nature.

3. Use the injected Clock for deterministic tests.

Do NOT use Thread.sleep(1100) in TC-RATE-006.

Production should use:

    Clock.systemUTC()

Tests should provide a controllable/mutable Clock and advance it beyond the
configured window.

Keep the test Clock implementation small and test-scoped where possible.

TC-RATE-006 should:

    exhaust quota
    advance test clock beyond the window
    verify next mutation succeeds

No real waiting.

4. HandlerInterceptor is approved.

Limit only these persistent Area mutation operations:

    POST   /workspaces/{workspaceId}/areas
    PUT    /workspaces/{workspaceId}/areas/{areaId}
    DELETE /workspaces/{workspaceId}/areas/{areaId}
    POST   /workspaces/{workspaceId}/areas/{areaId}/versions/{version}/restore

GET requests must not consume quota.

Be careful that path-based interceptor registration does not accidentally
rate-limit a future unrelated POST under /areas/**.

If necessary, make the interceptor explicitly recognize the currently
supported mutation routes/methods rather than relying only on
POST/PUT/DELETE + broad path matching.

5. Per-user identity remains JWT sub / User UUID.

No manual JWT parsing.

6. Fixed-window algorithm is approved for the single-instance prototype.

Default:

    max-actions: 50
    window: PT1M

7. HTTP 429 + RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED + Retry-After is approved.

Retry-After should represent the number of seconds until the current fixed
